# Phase 1: Base configuration and addressing

**Goal:** every device has a hostname, a loopback and working point-to-point links.

## CORE1 (NE40E)

```
<HUAWEI> system-view
[HUAWEI] sysname CORE1
[CORE1] interface LoopBack0
[CORE1-LoopBack0] ip address 10.255.0.1 32
[CORE1-LoopBack0] quit
[CORE1] interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0
[CORE1-GigabitEthernet1/0/0] undo shutdown
[CORE1-GigabitEthernet1/0/0] ip address 10.0.12.1 30
[CORE1-GigabitEthernet1/0/0] quit
[CORE1] interface GigabitEthernet1/0/1
[CORE1-GigabitEthernet1/0/1] undo shutdown
[CORE1-GigabitEthernet1/0/1] ip address 10.0.1.1 30
[CORE1-GigabitEthernet1/0/1] quit
[CORE1] interface GigabitEthernet1/0/2
[CORE1-GigabitEthernet1/0/2] undo shutdown
[CORE1-GigabitEthernet1/0/2] ip address 10.0.2.1 30
```

## CORE2 (NE40E)

Same pattern: loopback `10.255.0.2/32`, CORE1 link `10.0.12.2/30`, SW1 link `10.0.3.1/30`, SW2 link `10.0.4.1/30`.

## SW1 (CE12800) routed uplinks

Replace the example ports with the ports you cabled.

```
<HUAWEI> system-view
[HUAWEI] sysname SW1
[SW1] interface LoopBack0
[SW1-LoopBack0] ip address 10.255.0.11 32
[SW1-LoopBack0] quit
[SW1] interface GE1/0/1
[SW1-GE1/0/1] undo portswitch
[SW1-GE1/0/1] ip address 10.0.1.2 30
[SW1-GE1/0/1] quit
[SW1] interface GE1/0/2
[SW1-GE1/0/2] undo portswitch
[SW1-GE1/0/2] ip address 10.0.3.2 30
```

SW2: loopback `10.255.0.12/32`, uplinks `10.0.2.2/30` (CORE1) and `10.0.4.2/30` (CORE2).

## Verify

```
display ip interface brief
ping 10.0.12.2
ping 10.0.1.1
```

Expected: every directly connected neighbour replies.

